808 0 obj
<<
/Title (Warehouses were treated as supplier or distribution partners. Regions represented transport zones, and shipping modes represented delivery service types. We estimated transportation cost using distance, fuel price, shipping mode, and traffic index.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 795 0 R
/Next 809 0 R
>>
endobj
809 0 obj
<<
/Title (The supplier ranking showed that Warehouse_E had the highest reliability score, while Warehouse_S had the lowest reliability. Transportation analysis showed that West and South routes were more expensive and riskier, especially with Same Day and Second Class shipping. We also identified logistics bottlenecks and high-risk supply chain routes.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 795 0 R
/Prev 808 0 R
>>
endobj
810 0 obj
<<
/Title (Linear Regression, Random Forest Regressor, ARIMA, and Prophet)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 806 0 R
/Next 814 0 R
>>
endobj
811 0 obj
<<
/Title (Store numbers were grouped into regions. Each region was connected to a warehouse. Store type was used as a proxy for shipping mode. Weekly sales level was used to define order priority. Traffic index was estimated using fuel price, holiday weeks, and sales pressure.)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 806 0 R
/Prev 815 0 R
>>
endobj
812 0 obj
<<
/Title (Delivery delay prediction)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 806 0 R
