816 0 obj
<<
/Title (Then we created the Delivery Delay target using the logistic probability formula. We trained three models: Logistic Regression, Decision Tree, and Random Forest Classifier. The results showed that Traffic Index, fuel price, holiday weeks, distance, and sales pressure were the main delay drivers. This helps identify high-risk delivery routes.)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 812 0 R
>>
endobj
817 0 obj
<<
/Title (ABC Analysis showed that Category A departments generated around 79.33% of total sales. This means a small group of departments is responsible for most of the revenue. These departments should be monitored more carefully.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 813 0 R
/Next 818 0 R
>>
endobj
818 0 obj
<<
/Title (K-Means Clustering grouped departments based on total sales, average weekly sales, demand volatility, store coverage, and average markdown. We also identified overstock and understock risks and calculated reorder points using average weekly demand, lead time, and safety stock.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 813 0 R
/Prev 817 0 R
>>
endobj
819 0 obj
<<
/Title (ARIMA and Prophet)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 815 0 R
>>
